#
# Traces turn-38's two independent claims — closes clean, the fourth
# Pattern-grain act in this kernel to do so on the first attempt (after
# turn-17, turn-23, turn-27), for the now-familiar reason: the two-instance
# material was already on hand from turn-36's individual anchoring.
#
# Checked directly: both claims in turn-38 read the identical value,
# "signal (magnitude-anomaly), not noise," bound to independently-anchored
# entities. What this earns is a second PARADIGM — distinct from turn-23's
# ("signal, not noise" for absence-recurrence) — holding for the
